package ledgerkb

// corpus returns the synthetic LEDGERWORKS policy set. Every figure below is
// invented for the course; none describes a real regulation or company.
func corpus() []Doc {
	return []Doc{
		{ID: "REF-001", Title: "Refund policy", Body: "Scope: how LEDGERWORKS handles refund requests raised by merchants through the payments-support channel and the merchant portal. Owner: Disputes team. Rules: refunds go back to the original payment method and are processed within 5 business days. A refund above 2,500 EUR needs a second approval from a Compliance Officer. Merchants may request a refund up to 120 days after the original transaction; after 120 days the case moves to manual review by the Disputes team."},
		{ID: "CHB-002", Title: "Chargeback handling", Body: "Scope: the process for card chargebacks received from acquirers, covering evidence collection and merchant communication. Owner: Risk Operations. Rules: merchant evidence is due within 7 calendar days of the chargeback notice, because the acquirer deadline is 10 days. A chargeback fee of 15 EUR is charged to the merchant. Reason code 4837 (no cardholder authorization) is handled by the Fraud team, all other codes by Disputes."},
		{ID: "PAY-003", Title: "Payout schedule", Body: "Scope: when and how settled funds are paid out to merchant bank accounts in supported currencies. Owner: Treasury. Rules: standard payout is T+2 business days with a 14:00 Kyiv time cut-off. Instant payout is optional and costs 1.0% of the payout amount. The minimum payout is 10 EUR. A payout held for a risk review is released within 24 hours after clearance. All tariffs use the same payout schedule."},
		{ID: "PCI-004", Title: "PCI DSS scope and controls", Body: "Scope: the cardholder-data environment of LEDGERWORKS and the evidence the annual audit asks for. Owner: Security. Rules: LEDGERWORKS is validated as a PCI DSS Level 1 service provider. Card numbers are never written to logs; they are replaced by tokens issued by the internal tokenvault service. Quarterly ASV scans are mandatory, and the annual ROC audit is held in March."},
		{ID: "KYC-005", Title: "Merchant onboarding KYC", Body: "Scope: identity and business verification that every new merchant passes before the first payout. Owner: Compliance. Rules: merchants expecting more than 500,000 EUR monthly volume get enhanced due diligence. Beneficial owners are identified from 25% ownership. KYC documents are valid for 12 months. Review cycles by risk tier: low 24 months, medium 12 months, high 6 months."},
		{ID: "FX-006", Title: "FX and settlement currencies", Body: "Scope: currency conversion for merchants who accept payments in a currency other than their settlement currency. Owner: Treasury. Rules: settlement currencies are EUR, USD and UAH. The FX margin is 0.8% over the mid-market rate. Rates are fixed once a day at 10:00 Kyiv time. UAH settlements are reported to the regulator by Compliance."},
		{ID: "INC-007", Title: "Incident severity and response", Body: "Scope: how production incidents are classified and communicated across Engineering and Support. Owner: SRE. Rules: SEV1 means payouts are down or data is exposed; on-call is paged within 5 minutes, status updates go out every 30 minutes, and the post-mortem is due within 5 business days. SEV2 means a degraded service; page within 15 minutes, updates every 60 minutes, post-mortem within 10 business days."},
		{ID: "RET-008", Title: "Data retention schedule", Body: "Scope: how long each class of record is kept before deletion, and who may extend it. Owner: Legal. Rules: transaction records are kept 7 years. Call recordings are kept 90 days. Application logs are kept 30 days. Merchant KYC files are kept 5 years after offboarding. Agent audit entries follow the transaction-record rule of 7 years."},
		{ID: "AGT-009", Title: "AI agent operations policy", Body: "Scope: the limits that apply to any autonomous agent acting on LEDGERWORKS systems. Owner: Compliance. Rules: an agent may not approve a refund above 500 EUR on its own. Every agent action needs an audit entry. A change to an agent's strategy file needs human review by Compliance within 2 business days. An autonomous run is capped at 20 tool calls."},
		{ID: "FEE-010", Title: "Merchant fee schedule", Body: "Scope: the published price list for card processing and the conditions that change it. Owner: Commercial. Rules: the Standard tariff is 2.9% + 0.30 EUR per transaction. The Growth tariff is 2.4% + 0.25 EUR and applies above 100,000 EUR monthly volume. Enterprise pricing is custom. High-risk merchants have a rolling reserve of 5% held for 180 days."},
		{ID: "SLA-011", Title: "Support SLAs and escalation", Body: "Scope: response-time commitments to merchants and the escalation path when they are missed. Owner: Support. Rules: a P1 ticket gets a first response within 15 minutes, 24x7. A P2 ticket gets one within 4 hours on business days, a P3 within 2 business days. After two SLA breaches in one calendar month the account is escalated to the Head of Payments."},
	}
}
